{
  "title": "Taweez against Toothache",
  "data": "Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said: As for those who suffer from toothache, they may put their hands on the aching place and recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5), [Surah al-Tawhid](A116), [Surah al-Qadr](A101), and the following holy verse:\nوَتَرَى الْجِبَالَ تَحْسَبُهَا جَامِدَةً وَهِىَ تَمُرُّ مَرَّ السَّحَابِ\nWA TARAL JIBAALA TAHSABUHAA JAAMIDATAN WA HIYA TAMURRU MARRAS SAHAAB\nAnd you see the mountains, you think them firmly fixed, while they pass away as the passing of the cloud;\nصُنْعَ اللّٰهِ الَّذِىْ اَتْقَنَ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ اِنَّهٗ خَبِيْرٌ بِمَا تَفْعَلُوْنَ\nSUN'ALLAAHIL LADHEE ATQANA KULLA SHAY'IN INNAHOO KHABEERUN BIMAA TAF'ALOON\nthe handiwork of Allah, Who has made everything thoroughly; surely He is Aware of what you do. (27:88)\nLikewise, Imam Ali (a.s.) is reported to have said: You may rub the place of your prostration (in ritual prayers) with your hand, rub the aching tooth with it, and say the following:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ وَالشَّافِى اللّٰهُ وَلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَلِىِّ الْعَظِيْمِ\nBISMILLAAHI WASH SHAAFILLAAHU WA LAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A'LIYYIL A'ZEEM\nIn the Name of Allah; Allah is the Healer, and there is no power and no strength save in Allah, the Most High, the Great.\nAnother Taweez against Toothache\nYou may recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116), saying with each of them:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMILLAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful.\nAfter Surah al-Tawhid, you may recite the following holy verses:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ وَلَهٗ مَا سَكَنَ فِى اللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ\nBISMILLAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEMI WA LAHOO MAA SAKANA FIL LAYLI WAN NAHAARI WA HUWAS SAMEE'UL A'LEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful. And to Him belongs whatever dwells in the night and the day; and He is the Hearing, the Knowing. (6:13)\nقُلْنَا يَا نَارُ كُوْنِىْ بَرْدًا وَسَلَامًا عَلٰى اِبْرَاهِيْمَ وَاَرَادُوْا بِهٖ كَيْدًا فَجَعَلْنَاهُمُ الْاَخْسَرِيْنَ\nQULNAA YAA NAARU KOONEE BARDAN WA SALAAMAN A'LAA IBRAAHEEMA WA ARAADOO BIHEE KAYDAN FAJA'ALNAAHUMUL AKHSAREEN\nWe said: O fire! be coolness and peace upon Ibrahim. And they intended a plan against him, but We made them the greater losers. (21:69-70)\nنُوْدِىَ اَنْ بُوْرِكَ مَنْ فِى النَّارِ وَمَنْ حَوْلَهَا وَسُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nNOODIYA AN BOORIKA MAN FIN NAARI WA MAN HAWLAHAA WA SUBHAANALLAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN\nA voice was uttered, saying: Blessed is whoever is in the fire and whoever is about it; and glory be to Allah, the Lord of the worlds. (27:8)\nYou may then say the following supplicatory prayer:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ يَا كَافِيًا مِّنْ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ وَلَا يَكْفِىْ مِنْكَ شَيْءٌ\nALLAAHUMMA YAA KAAFIYAM MIN KULLI SHAY'IN WA LAA YAKFEE MINKA SHAY'\nO Allah, O He Who suffices against everything, while nothing suffices against You,\nاِكْفِ عَبْدَكَ وَابْنَ اَمَتِكَ مِنْ شَرِّ مَا يُخَافُ وَيُحْذَرُ\nIKFI A'BDAKA WABNA AMATIKA MIN SHARRI MAA YUKHAAFU WA YUHDHAR\nsuffice Your servant, the son of Your bondwoman, against the evil of what is feared and guarded against,\nوَمِنْ شَرِّ الْوَجَعِ الَّذِىْ يَشْكُوْهُ اِلَيْكَ\nWA MIN SHARRIL WAJA'IL LADHEE YASHKOOHU ILAYK\nand against the evil of the pain that he complains of to You.\nIt is also reported that one who suffers from toothache may take a blade or a leaf of a date-palm tree, rub the aching place with it, and repeat the following seven times:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ بِسْمِ اللّٰهِ وَبِاللّٰهِ مُحَمَّدٌ رَّسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ وَاِبْرَاهِيْمُ خَلِيْلُ اللّٰهِ\nBISMILLAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEMI BISMILLAAHI WA BILLAAHI MUHAMMADUR RASOOLULLAAHI WA IBRAAHEEMU KHALEELULLAAH\nIn the Name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful. In the Name of Allah and by Allah; Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and Ibrahim is the Friend of Allah.\nاُسْكُنْ بِالَّذِىْ سَكَنَ لَهٗ مَا فِى اللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ بِاِذْنِهٖ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nUSKUN BILLADHEE SAKANA LAHOO MAA FIL LAYLI WAN NAHAARI BI-IDHNIHEE WA HUWA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nBe still, by Him for Whom whatever is in the night and the day is still, by His permission; and He has power over all things.\nIt is also reported that one who suffers from toothache may put a stick or a piece of iron on the tooth and recite this amulet over it seven times:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ اَلْعَجَبُ كُلُّ الْعَجَبِ دُوْدَةٌ تَكُوْنُ فِى الْفَمِ تَاْكُلُ الْعَظْمَ وَتُنْزِلُ الدَّمَ\nBISMILLAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEMIL A'JABU KULLUL A'JABI DOODATUN TAKOONU FIL FAMI TA'KULUL A'ZMA WA TUNZILUD DAM\nIn the Name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful. How strange, how very strange: a worm in the mouth that eats the bone and brings down the blood!\nاَنَا الرَّاقِىْ وَاللّٰهُ الشَّافِىْ وَالْكَافِىْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nANAR RAAQEE WALLAAHUSH SHAAFEE WAL KAAFEE LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAL HAMDU LILLAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN\nI am the one who recites the charm, and Allah is the Healer and the Sufficer. There is no god but Allah, and all praise is due to Allah, the Lord of the worlds.\nوَاِذْ قَتَلْتُمْ نَفْسًا فَادَّارَاْتُمْ فِيْهَا وَاللّٰهُ مُخْرِجٌ مَّا كُنْتُمْ تَكْتُمُوْنَ\nWA IDH QATALTUM NAFSAN FADDAARA'TUM FEEHAA WALLAAHU MUKHRIJUM MAA KUNTUM TAKTUMOON\nAnd when you killed a man, then you disagreed with respect to that, and Allah was to bring forth that which you were going to hide.\nفَقُلْنَا اضْرِبُوْهُ بِبَعْضِهَا كَذٰلِكَ يُحْيِى اللّٰهُ الْمَوْتٰى وَيُرِيْكُمْ اٰيَاتِهٖ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُوْنَ\nFAQULNAD RIBOOHU BIBA'DIHAA KADHAALIKA YUHYILLAAHUL MAWTAA WA YUREEKUM AAYAATIHEE LA'ALLAKUM TA'QILOON\nSo We said: Strike the dead body with part of it. Thus Allah brings the dead to life, and He shows you His signs so that you may understand. (2:72-73)\nThe whole amulet may be repeated seven times."
